		{"id":"e478a795281620dd","type":"text","text":"handleOutput` ( Pendiente de ser verificado)","x":-130,"y":0,"width":245,"height":60},
		{"id":"b03a65f0d3196537","type":"text","text":"Device","x":80,"y":-140,"width":140,"height":60},
		{"id":"a4303cb7f6cc5cb3","type":"text","text":"Anulan","x":-185,"y":169,"width":130,"height":50},
		{"id":"792ef8f7b927172b","type":"text","text":"Otros : Sample, Events ...","x":115,"y":437,"width":160,"height":58},
		{"id":"67b10b69199e36aa","type":"text","text":"Ejemplo el dispositivo se queda sin cobertura y al recuperarla este ahora tiene otra ip y al reconectarse este lo primero que haria seria enviar los datos acumulados","x":480,"y":368,"width":241,"height":197},
		{"id":"58c4cd017fb12b65","type":"text","text":"Confirm","x":115,"y":219,"width":105,"height":50},
		{"id":"f7aeb8ac2f7066e2","type":"text","text":"Rejected","x":115,"y":319,"width":105,"height":50},
		{"id":"a2a0fb88862df9b4","type":"text","text":"[[AKO 44 - Flujo de cambio de parámetros Cloud - Device.canvas]]","x":-1174,"y":-420,"width":297,"height":78},
		{"id":"be426b2d49d9ca00","type":"text","text":"CMD [ 530, 2]","x":-410,"y":-28,"width":140,"height":57},
		{"id":"d4f2417d3f9f34a1","type":"text","text":"PendingOutput Anulado","x":123,"y":-411,"width":245,"height":60},
		{"id":"a9d2ceba91498e0e","type":"text","text":"Mensaje de Audit","x":-185,"y":-411,"width":180,"height":60},
		{"id":"5113ef329fd541ee","x":-535,"y":-402,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"`initializeAuditProcessor`"},
		{"id":"1c358a70e0a63379","x":-567,"y":-680,"width":314,"height":128,"type":"text","text":"`akocloud-micros/src/micros/backlog.perte/bl-lib/services/AuditProcessor.ts`\n"},
		{"id":"e67e8263d62b372c","type":"text","text":"si status = pending & param_lic_sys_state =  2 = 2","x":117,"y":-666,"width":317,"height":100},
		{"id":"e937f1315240b810","x":-185,"y":438,"width":120,"height":58,"type":"text","text":"Retry x 3"},
		{"id":"8b37189f927fd1e6","type":"text","text":"ACK","x":340,"y":-22,"width":80,"height":52},
		{"id":"64ab68cae9d1d2a1","x":1471,"y":-152,"width":409,"height":212,"type":"text","text":"PI (sendConfig12830)\n  → AMQP: \"backlog.12830.input\"\n    → backlog.mediator → statecontroller (crea backlog PENDING)\n      → AMQP: \"driver.output.12830\"\n        → translator.perte :: handleOutput()"},
		{"id":"dfca41d924be38bf","x":1200,"y":-340,"width":366,"height":89,"type":"text","text":"### 1. Primer envío (API → Device)"},
		{"id":"ff0d2f5c74f763f9","x":1500,"y":160,"width":380,"height":144,"type":"text","text":"Que hace handleOutput\n\n`translator.perte handleOutput`\n1. **Parsea** el mensaje del backlog\n2. **Convierte** los parámetros a formato CoAP (registros MODBUS del dispositivo)\n3. **Guarda** en MongoDB con `storeOutput()` → crea documento en `outputMsg` con status `PENDING`\n4. **Envía** por primera vez: `sendEvent(\"cl.output.perte.coap.driver\", toCLMessage)` → esto baja al CL (Communication Layer) que envía por CoAP al dispositivo"},
		{"id":"a81443065256286e","x":2028,"y":299,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"El translator **no se queda esperando** una respuesta síncrona. Simplemente deja el mensaje como `PENDING` en la BD y termina."},
		{"id":"e25220e269e3b062","x":2456,"y":234,"width":364,"height":206,"type":"text","text":"### 2. \"Esperar\" la respuesta (polling pasivo)\n\nEl sistema **no espera activamente**. Lo que hace es un mecanismo de **reintento por piggyback**:\n\nCada vez que el dispositivo envía **cualquier mensaje** (sample, sync, status, etc.), entra por\n\n`handleInput`\n\n(línea 55). Si el mensaje **NO es** un\n\n`CMD_ACK`\n\nni\n\n`PARAM_ACK`\n\n, el código en las líneas 134-152 se ejecuta:"},
		{"id":"3f85b9f358e97217","x":2989,"y":268,"width":391,"height":252,"type":"text","text":"Device envía un sample/sync/status/etc.\n  → AMQP: \"driver.input.perte\"  \n    → translator.perte :: handleInput()\n      → Procesa el mensaje normalmente\n      → ADEMÁS, busca pending: getPendingOutputMessage()\n        → Si hay PENDING → reenvía el comando al device\n        → updateRetries() incrementa contador\n          → Si max_retries → emite \"12830.output.failed\" y cancela\n          → Si no → sendEvent(\"cl.output.perte.coap.driver\", outputMsg)"},
		{"id":"9d28fe1a485511dc","x":3604,"y":306,"width":476,"height":234,"type":"text","text":"### 3. Confirmación (Device → Translator)\n\nCuando el dispositivo **aplica** los cambios, envía un `cmd_ack`\n\n```js\n{ \"id\": [974130021, 6000, 1, 26, 0], \"ty\": \"cmd_ack\", \"bid\": 12345 }\n```\n\nEsto entra por\n\n`handleInput`\n\n(líneas 108-122):"},
		{"id":"19345539d93a5f84","x":137,"y":77,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Script `client-perte`\n```js\nnode bin/examples/client-perte.js 974130021 <uuid> cmd_ack -v\n```"}
	],
